{"result":{"atchFileId":"FILE_900000000007142","bbsId":"BBSMSTR_000000000081","bbsIds":null,"frstRegisterId":"USRCNFRM_00000000000","frstRegisterPnttm":"2017-12-15","lastUpdusrId":"","lastUpdusrPnttm":"","ntceBgnde":"2017-12-30          ","ntceEndde":"9999-11-30          ","ntcrId":"","ntcrNm":"","nttCn":"<p>태안 마도해역 탐사보고서의 후속보고서로 2011~2012년, 2014년의 시굴&middot;탐사조사의 내용이 실려 있습니다. 마도해역은 수중문화재의 보고(寶庫)로서, 태안선과 마도1, 2, 3, 4호선 등 고려~조선시대 난파선 5척이 조사되었습니다. 이러한 고선박의 발굴은 시굴&middot;탐사조사가 그 밑거름이 되어 이루어진 성과라고 할 수 있습니다. 보고서는 Ⅰ. 머리말 / Ⅱ. 조사방법 및 내용 / Ⅲ. 출수유물 / Ⅳ. 맺음말 / 초록(국영중일문) 등으로 구성하였습니다. *담당부서 : 수중발굴과</p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>","nttCnEn":"<p>The National Research Institute of Maritime Cultural Heritage has been carrying out extensive research on shipwrecks since 2008. Investigations on the Taean Treasure ship, a sunken vessel from the Goryeo Dynasty (918&ndash;1392), were followed from 2009 to 2011 by research on Mado Shipwrecks No. 1, 2, and 3. Additionally, the the first vessel from the Joseon Dynasty(1392 &ndash; 1910), Mado Shipwreck No. 4, was examined in 2015. The Mado waters&mdash;referred to as Nanhaengryang (難行梁, literally, &ldquo;hard to pass bank&rdquo;) for their rough nature&mdash;have long been regarded as one of the top four most treacherous maritime routes in Korea. As the location of numerous shipwrecks, however, these coastal waters have become a treasure trove of maritime cultural history. The discovery of ancient ships has been achieved through prospectings and excavations. This publication is a follow-up report to the earlier published survey report on the Mado waters. It includes detailed information on the prospectings and excavations conducted from 2011 to 2012 and again in 2014.</p>","nttCn2":"","nttCn3":"","nttCn4":"","nttCn5":"","nttCn6":"","nttCn7":"","categoryDetailCode":"ACARPT001","categoryDetailCode2":"","nttId":1250,"nttNo":1,"nttSj":"태안 마도해역 시굴조사 보고서","nttSjEn":"Waters off the Taean-Mado Underwater Excavation","parnts":"0","password":"","inqireCo":5013,